}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 7 "det(C);" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "
" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 111 "Donc, C n'est pas
 inversible et les vecteurs [1,2,3], [4,5,6] et [7,8,9] sont lin\351ai
rement d\351pendants dans R^3." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 85 "En fait, si on calcule la forme \351chelo
nn\351e r\351duite selon les lignes de C, on obtient:" }}{PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "rref(C);" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 277 "Ainsi, u
ne solution du syst\350me C * (a,b,c)^t = (0,0,0)^t est donn\351e par \+
(a,b,c)=(s,-2s,s) avec s dans dans les r\351els. Donc, s*[1,2,3] + (-2
s)*[4,5,6] + (s)*[7,8,9] = [0,0,0]. On voit alors, en prenant s = 1 qu
e [7,8,9] = (-1)*[1,2,3] + (2)*[4,5,6], d'o\371 la d\351pendance lin
\351aire." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 1 " " }{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 13 "transpose(C);" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 7 "det(%);" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "
" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 52 "Cela v\351rifie la
 relation det(C) = det(C_transpos\351e)." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 72 "On peut aussi calculer les valeurs
 propres et les vecteurs propres de C." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "
" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 15 "eigenvalues(C);" }{TEXT -1 0 "
" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 17 "eigenvectors(C); " }{TEXT -1 
